Subject: StandardBackendUpdater: keep a failed update listed on the Updates page

A transaction that ends in DoneWithErrorStatus was reported to the
Updates page as Done. The page filters out rows whose state is done, and
UpdateModel keeps the same rows when the list of offered resources does
not change, which it does not after a refused or failed update: the page
listed nothing, with Update All still enabled, until a refresh. A failed
transaction now reports None, as a cancelled one does.

--- a/libdiscover/resources/StandardBackendUpdater.cpp
+++ b/libdiscover/resources/StandardBackendUpdater.cpp
@@ -120,13 +120,17 @@
     case Transaction::SetupStatus:
     case Transaction::QueuedStatus:
     case Transaction::CancelledStatus:
+    // A failed update leaves its resource where it was. Done would keep the
+    // Updates page's row filtered out (resourceStateIsDone) while the
+    // resource is still offered, and the page would list nothing until a
+    // refresh made new rows.
+    case Transaction::DoneWithErrorStatus:
         return AbstractBackendUpdater::None;
     case Transaction::DownloadingStatus:
         return AbstractBackendUpdater::Downloading;
     case Transaction::CommittingStatus:
         return AbstractBackendUpdater::Installing;
     case Transaction::DoneStatus:
-    case Transaction::DoneWithErrorStatus:
         return AbstractBackendUpdater::Done;
     }
     Q_UNREACHABLE();
